5
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:16,909
Choose that named form.

6
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:20,909
Read the available name and category
before starting; your own

7
00:00:20,909 --> 00:00:24,239
department may offer a different
collection of forms for its work.

8
00:00:24,379 --> 00:00:28,530
The selected form says This form is filled
in online only.

9
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:32,759
In Details, Summary has an asterisk and
Notes provides

10
00:00:32,759 --> 00:00:34,490
space for the longer explanation.

11
00:00:34,979 --> 00:00:37,540
Read those labels before entering
information.

12
00:00:37,929 --> 00:00:42,139
A clear summary helps another authorized
operator recognize the record later,

13
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:44,610
while notes carry the supporting detail.

14
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:48,949
Save and send is the action below the
fields for this online example.

15
00:00:49,149 --> 00:00:52,649
Enter a concise Summary and Notes for the
software exercise.

16
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:58,489
The example summary begins Training Only
and describes an IC coordination handover.

17
00:00:58,979 --> 00:01:02,010
Review both fields, then choose Save and
send.

18
00:01:02,519 --> 00:01:05,890
The returned record page has a draft
reference at the top and a

19
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:07,689
Draft tag beneath the form name.

20
00:01:08,179 --> 00:01:10,279
Read those together with your saved text.

21
00:01:10,689 --> 00:01:13,630
This is the working draft you can review
before finalizing.

22
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:18,280
While the record is a draft, update Notes
with a clear practice revision.

23
00:01:18,789 --> 00:01:23,199
Here the added sentence begins Training
Update and says the handover note

24
00:01:23,199 --> 00:01:25,039
was reviewed for software practice.

25
00:01:25,510 --> 00:01:26,430
Choose Save.

26
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:31,020
The verified draft still shows that update
in Notes, retains the original

27
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,260
Summary and remains marked Draft.

28
00:01:33,639 --> 00:01:38,049
Compare the saved text with the change you
intended before moving on to completion.

29
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:44,040
Read I attest this Record is complete and
accurate before selecting its checkbox.

30
00:01:44,549 --> 00:01:47,300
Finalize is initially disabled in this
example.

31
00:01:47,830 --> 00:01:52,410
After reviewing this fictional software
record, the author selects the attestation

32
00:01:52,469 --> 00:01:54,229
and Finalize becomes available.

33
00:01:54,639 --> 00:01:57,510
Treat that as a deliberate completion
decision based on

34
00:01:57,510 --> 00:01:59,160
the actual record contents.

35
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:02,760
For practice, compare the unchecked and
selected states

36
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,590
before choosing the final action.

37
00:02:04,859 --> 00:02:07,490
Choose Finalize for the reviewed practice
record.

38
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:12,390
The returned page shows Finalized and the
header now reads I C note,

39
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:15,110
twenty twenty-six, zero zero zero one.

40
00:02:15,529 --> 00:02:18,440
Its Summary and Notes are displayed
read-only, and the

41
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:20,150
draft editing actions are gone.

42
00:02:20,659 --> 00:02:23,709
Verify the state and number as the result
of completion.

43
00:02:24,129 --> 00:02:27,560
The earlier draft reference and the final
record number identify

44
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,869
different stages of this same example.

45
00:02:30,029 --> 00:02:32,240
Use Back to return to Records.

46
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:37,119
Under Recent, find the same record number
and the coordination handover summary,

47
00:02:37,369 --> 00:02:39,239
with the Finalized tag on the right.

48
00:02:39,619 --> 00:02:42,829
An unrelated Work record remains in Drafts
above it.

49
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:47,409
Read the section, number, summary and
state together when selecting

50
00:02:47,409 --> 00:02:51,370
a record; completing one item does not
mean that every draft in

51
00:02:51,370 --> 00:02:52,969
the workspace has been completed.

52
00:02:53,229 --> 00:02:57,039
This workflow can document a security
supervisor handover, a

53
00:02:57,039 --> 00:03:01,049
search-and-rescue coordination exercise, a
community paramedicine

54
00:03:01,129 --> 00:03:05,170
or mental health team handover, wildland
contractor coordination,

55
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:09,820
industrial response exercises, or fire and
E M S department work.

56
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:13,480
The form fields and responsibilities
should match your department.

57
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:17,480
The repeatable pattern is to choose the
correct form, review the

58
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:22,099
